                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I\u2019ve seen firsthand the devastation hurricanes leave behind, families picking up the pieces after losing everything. In those moments, the last thing they should worry about is whether their flood insurance will come through.\n\nThat\u2019s why I\u2019m proud to support H.R. 5574, led by Congressman Ezell, to keep the National Flood Insurance Program funded during the Schumer Shutdown. While Democrats play politics, we\u2019re making sure disaster victims aren\u2019t left behind. Keeping NFIP alive means keeping our word, and putting people over politics.",
